.TH STARTNOW 1 "August 2026" "startnow 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
startnow \- Ninite-style developer tool installer for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B startnow
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B startnow
is a terminal UI installer for developer tools. Select tools from the
catalog, and it downloads, verifies (sha256) and installs them reliably.
Supported install styles: direct archives from official sources, official
installer scripts, and native system packages via the distro's package
manager (APT, DNF, Pacman, Zypper, APK).
.SH TABS
Tools, Machine, Usage. Switch with TAB or 1-3, or click the tab pills.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B up/down, j/k
move in the tools table
.TP
.B space
toggle selection
.TP
.B a
select all / clear
.TP
.B /
focus the filter (or click it)
.TP
.B v
set a pinned version
.TP
.B u
check for / install updates
.TP
.B x
uninstall a managed tool
.TP
.B i
tool details (or right-click a row)
.TP
.B enter
install selected tools
.TP
.B ?
full help
.TP
.B q, ctrl+c
quit
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.startnow/bin
symlinks to installed binaries; add to PATH
.TP
.I ~/.startnow/manifest.json
tools installed by startnow and their versions
.TP
.I ~/.cache/startnow
downloaded archives
.SH SEE ALSO
Go (https://go.dev), Bubble Tea (https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea)
